%=========================================================================
\section{Methodology}
\label{sec:methodology}
%=========================================================================

\subsection{Pattern Taxonomy}

We study 13 coordination patterns plus a single-agent baseline organized into six categories (Figure~\ref{fig:taxonomy}). Each multi-agent pattern is parameterized by agent count $n$ and shares a common termination vocabulary (\texttt{TERMINATE} keyword for graceful stopping, \texttt{max\_messages}=25 as safety bound). The single-agent baseline (Category~S) provides a reference point for quantifying coordination overhead. Table~\ref{tab:patterns} details the configurations.

